---
// "Built on our own round": a left-aligned editorial block in Grant's voice, with no image (0025).
// The copy is a draft for Grant to rewrite (0014). It states only what PanePilot's docs confirm.
// The claim about where it is hosted stays out until Grant says where the database lives (0025).
---

<section id="story" class="container story" aria-labelledby="story-heading">
  <h2 id="story-heading">Built on our own round</h2>
  <div class="story__text">
    <p>
      We clean windows in South Australia's Clare Valley, and I built PanePilot to run our round. It quotes per pane because
      that's how we price. It runs from a phone because that's where we are when the visit's done. It pays our workers for
      the time they log, because that's how we pay them.
    </p>
    <p class="story__quiet">
      Each business sees only its own customers, prices and money.
    </p>
    <a class="story__link" href="https://panepilot.au">See PanePilot at panepilot.au</a>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .story {
    display: grid;
    gap: 20px;
    padding-block: clamp(56px, 8vw, 96px);
  }

  .story h2 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(28px, 5vw, 36px);
  }

  .story__text {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 16px;
    max-width: 38rem;
  }

  .story__text p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 19px;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  /* Quiet on Paper, 9.6:1. */
  .story__text .story__quiet {
    color: var(--site-text-quiet);
  }

  .story__link {
    font-weight: 600;
    text-underline-offset: 4px;
  }

  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .story {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 4fr) minmax(0, 7fr);
      gap: 56px;
    }
  }
</style>
